      "attack_scenario": "1) A proxy instance of `InitializableImmutableAdminUpgradeabilityProxy` is deployed on-chain (implementation is still unset).\n2) Before the legitimate deployer/admin sends the separate initialization transaction, an attacker monitors mempool / chain events and calls `initialize(attackerLogic, attackerInitCalldata)`.\n3) The proxy now delegates all future calls to `attackerLogic`. The attacker can implement functions to steal any ERC20/ETH later sent to or approved for the proxy, or to mimic expected interfaces while maliciously redirecting funds.\n4) Legitimate initialization attempts revert because the implementation is no longer unset, permanently hijacking the proxy instance.",
      "suggested_fix": "Ensure initialization cannot be performed by arbitrary callers:\n- Override `initialize` in this contract to require `msg.sender == _admin()` (immutable admin) before allowing initialization; and/or\n- Set implementation + run initialization from the constructor (custom proxy pattern) so it is impossible to deploy uninitialized; and/or\n- Only deploy via a factory that deploys and immediately calls `initialize` within the same transaction (atomic deployment), never leaving the proxy uninitialized on-chain."
